      "writtenOn": "2025-01-14T16:57:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It was with `emulator`. It turns out that arm64 Android emulators running on x86_64 have not been supported since Oreo. That\u0027s \"documented\" somewhere, but I don\u0027t have the link handy.\n\nI messed with this a lot last night for a personal use case. I rebuilt the emulator with this restriction manually removed (which requires a new repo checkout with `emu-35-5-release`). With the `-qemu -machine virt` args, it tried to start but segfaulted after trying to launch some render threads, so it didn\u0027t work and I gave up there for now.\n\ncuttlefish is apparently the new hotness and doesn\u0027t rely on a complicated qemu fork, but I\u0027m not sure if it would allow running arm64 on x86-64 either.",
      "parentUuid": "abde0ef0_f36e2ea6",
